invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_p256_point_on_curve inverts its branch, so the signer's
  on-curve check runs p256_wide_point_on_curve, on the native 64x64->128
  multiply, for every answer but WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME, and
  p256_point_on_curve on the decomposition for the one answer that states
  the multiply's timing. Every answer still comes out the same.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into each copy and requires
  the wide files alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        uint32_t on_curve = p256_wide_point_on_curve(x, y);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        uint32_t on_curve = p256_wide_point_on_curve(x, y);
